const faqs=[
  {q:'Has Malaysia hosted ATP or WTA tournaments?',a:'Yes. Kuala Lumpur hosted ATP tour events in 1993–1995 and the ATP 250 Malaysian Open from 2009 to 2015, plus WTA events in 1992 and from 2010 to 2017. There has been no ATP or WTA tour-level event in Malaysia since 2017.'},
  {q:'Who won the ATP Malaysian Open?',a:'Champions of the 2009–2015 ATP Malaysian Open were Nikolay Davydenko, Mikhail Youzhny, Janko Tipsarević, Juan Mónaco, João Sousa, Kei Nishikori and David Ferrer.'},
  {q:'Why did the Malaysian Open tennis tournaments end?',a:'After 2015 the ATP event’s place on the calendar went to Chengdu, China. The WTA event’s promoter chose not to continue after 2017, citing calendar changes and sponsorship difficulty, and the licence it had leased returned to Palermo.'},
  {q:'What professional tennis is played in Malaysia now?',a:'ITF World Tennis Tour events such as the M15 Kuala Lumpur tournaments, ITF junior events (including the J300 Premier Sarawak Cup and J200 Kuala Lumpur), and national team ties in the Davis Cup and Billie Jean King Cup. See our tournament calendar.'},
